# Devcontainer Tool Installation

When a new tool requires `sudo` to install inside the devcontainer:

1. Add the tool to `.devcontainer/Dockerfile` (and update `devcontainer.json` features if applicable) so future container rebuilds include it.
2. Return the install command to the user to run from the host for the current session.

Never run `sudo` directly in the agent session. Always persist the change in devcontainer configs and hand off the immediate install to the user.

```
# ❌ BAD — running sudo directly
sudo apt-get install -y helm

# ✅ GOOD — update Dockerfile + hand off
# 1. Add to .devcontainer/Dockerfile:
#    RUN apt-get update && apt-get install -y helm
# 2. Tell the user:
"I've added helm to the Dockerfile for future rebuilds. For now, please run:
  sudo apt-get update && sudo apt-get install -y helm"
```
